id: pm-6mjxgq
title: "GH-890: extension collision diagnostics omit the effective winner and cannot distinguish safe scoped overlap"
description: "GitHub issue #890 reproduces a 17-package workspace where renderer, parser, and preflight registrations collide. Health names contenders but not the effective winner, equal-priority tie-breaking is undocumented, and registration-time diagnostics cannot distinguish safe scoped renderer fallthrough from genuine shadowing. Package authors and agents therefore cannot act on twenty warnings without source inspection."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags[8]: agent-ux,"area:extensions","area:health","area:sdk",collision,determinism,github-report,packages
created_at: "2026-08-04T08:44:04.821Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-04T09:19:18.204Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 300
acceptance_criteria: The SDK defines deterministic priority and tie-break contracts for every override class and publishes them in contracts and package-author docs; Health and package doctor name the effective winner and explain resolution provenance for genuine collisions; Scoped renderer ownership declarations avoid false collision findings while an unscoped shadowing negative control still fails; The full published external package fleet has a documented expected-collision policy and a stable integration fixture
parent: pm-ugqx
risk: high
confidence: high
severity: high
environment: pm-cli 2026.8.3 with 17 published external pm packages installed in one project
repro_steps: "Install the package fleet from GitHub issue #890; run pm health --json; inspect extension_renderer_collision, extension_parser_override_collision, and extension_preflight_override_collision warnings"
expected_result: "Diagnostics identify deterministic resolution, explicit default priority, and safe scoped overlaps separately from genuine shadowing"
actual_result: "Warnings identify contenders only, health becomes not-ok with zero load or activation failures, and agents cannot tell which behavior is active"
customer_impact: A normal package-catalog installation trains agents to ignore health warnings or remove compatible packages
