comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-04T08:44:04.821Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check 2026-08-04: all-status searches covered extension collisions, scoped renderer ownership, winner selection, default priority, package doctor, and health. Closed pm-nf7q handled scoped renderer ownership in isolation, but no active item owns deterministic winner reporting plus equal-priority policy across the full external package fleet. GitHub source: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/890"
  "2026-08-04T09:19:18.204Z","harness:codex","External-fleet evidence 2026-08-04: the isolated npm registry smoke discovered and tested 18 published external packages, all at 2026.8.4, with init, install, deep package doctor, and runtime contracts passing for every package; activation failures=0 and blocking failures=0. The run still surfaces intentional/global override warnings, and pm-graph installation took about 22.8s of a 24.1s smoke while pm-ops completed in 3.9s. This fleet pass does not remove the collision/winner ambiguity reported by GitHub #890; it proves the current packages succeed in isolation, not when composed together."
body: ""
